# The upkeep trigger's intervening "if" (CR 603.4): Bot1 plays a Plains on turn one and Bot2 a Plains on turn two, so in Bot1's
# turn-three upkeep the opponent controls the same number of lands, not more, and the trigger does not go on the stack.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Discerning Financier
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Discerning Financier.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Plains; Discerning Financier
